{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1006490-how-to-st","id":1006490,"title":"How to ST?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-21T18:07:18-08:00","id":1006490,"title":"How to ST?","content":"So, one of my players decided to leave the training wheels behind and she decided to try to run a game. She is quite nervious and she is running against the clock (she has to ST a game for her friends on saturday) so.. considering all the years of experience we have accumulated in here.... Any advices for a new player?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T18:38:58-08:00","id":1006496,"title":"","content":"I'd start with Greg Stolze's &quot;How To Run Roleplaying Games&quot;, near the bottom of <a href=\"http://www.gregstolze.com/downloads.html\" target=\"_blank\">his downloads page</a>.<br /> <br /> Having a plot and some other material prepared can really help a new ST's confidence. Improvising is a skill STs learn, so having a straightforward adventure planned out can help.<br /> <br /> For a first time, I would suggest looking at published adventures. She might not want to run one as-is, but it can help to at least see what one looks like. I gave a <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> player who had STed a few sessions a copy of the original quickstart <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/8/Alien-Hunger\" target=\"_blank\">Alien Hunger</a> and she modified and ran it for friends recently. It's a bid odd, and uses first edition rules, but the first chapters in particular still work well as introductions to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T18:58:25-08:00","id":1006503,"title":"","content":"A few bits of wisdom<ul><li>When it comes to plots and characters, take and adapt everything.</li> <li>Remember that the rules and canon exist to help you have fun; if something is really being problematic and the group and ST agrees ignore it.<ul><li>Consider any changes beforehand though, try to figure out why it is whatever rule or bit of canon bothers you. If there is a deeper issue it might be worth confronting rather than simply discarding.</li> </ul></li> <li>Dont be afraid to make temporary rulings to keep the game flowing. Few things can ruin the flow of roleplay by having to stop the game for 10 minutes while you look something up.<ul><li>Generally allow 2-5 minutes at most to look something up. Past that point issue a temporary ruling until after the game at which point it can be looked up fully.</li> <li>Also dont be afraid to change a ruling if you should find out relevant data later.</li> </ul></li> <li>Dont be afraid to say no. If you are developing a story and you have certain restrictions on character creation, sometimes you have to say no to someone who want to do something too far out of range.<ul><li>In the same way Dont be afraid to say yes, just because someone wants to make something that doesnt quite fit the creation parameters doesnt mean it is absurd. Consider their ideas before you say no. Although as stated above if it is too much say no and then work with the player to adapt the idea into a more usable form.</li> </ul></li> <li>The World of Darkness is not our world. Dont get into contests over the minutia of a setting with the players, after a certain point you can point out that this your game and the world fits how you as the ST sees it.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T12:26:56-08:00","id":1006804,"title":"","content":"If you're running vampire. Set up the important players, but include some leeway for nuetrals that players can use or for new players that can be catered towards the player. For werewolf, You'll probably want to drift away from cutthroat politics to more DnD style sessions. Tribal conflict is interesting and oppresive, but it's not something that can be fought on a session by session basis. For mage. Well. A first time storyteller shouldn't run mage unless she's been playing it a lot. <br /> <br /> Don't have more than 5 players. three is probably the best amount. <br /> <br /> Don't be afraid to be an ass. In the world of darkness, things are pretty grim. Phyric victories, inconsequentual wins, a defeat where the players weren't looking. All of these are useful tools to establish the universe. Young garou,Neonates, apprentices, the like","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T00:49:21-08:00","id":1007086,"title":"","content":"Which game is she planning to run? Vampire? Werewolf? Mage?(!)<br /> <br /> It'll be easier to come up with tips if we know what sort of game she's setting up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:07:55-08:00","id":1007332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1006490-how-to-st?p=1007086#post1007086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which game is she planning to run? Vampire? Werewolf? Mage?(!)<br /> <br /> It'll be easier to come up with tips if we know what sort of game she's setting up.</div> </div> </div> </div>she is thinking about going with Werewolf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T12:00:17-08:00","id":1007359,"title":"","content":"All great advice above. I'd add: if she's nervous about a particular scene, just sandbox it, but give it some thought. Players might not like having their choices limited, but if there's a clever reason, it's become simple good storytelling. For anything else, improvisation is your friend, even if she doesn't see it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}